From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anothers <14343424+Anothers@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 02:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 94/94] dsv41: zero-spill sm_121 x3ld decode, fused expert
 rot_in, and RT=8 router prefetch

Decode staged trellis words directly from shared memory in x3ld via
32-bit __funnelshift_l windows (supporting LW2 <= 4 with static_assert
for K2=2..16 including K2=15), use qmm_frag::grid_wait() for PDL waits,
and vectorize the shared-memory warp reduction with float4 to eliminate
register spills on sm_121 K2=10/12 kernels. Under TF_DSV41_R1=1, select
pd=2 on 2-16 row windows when per_warp is even, fuse mat=0,1 in
rot_in_kernel, pack bf16 outputs via uint2 in store4_out, elide dead
s.ex.y writebacks in down_combine_kernel when fold is active without
x3ld_epi, and extend router_narrow XP=2 prefetching to RT <= 8.

Re-measures all 105 affected sm_121 contract entries across nvcc 13.0,
13.2, and 13.3 without dropping 13.2/13.3 coverage, and expands
x3ld_epi_bench.zig to widths 2..12 plus direct grouped_kernel parity.
